Hi Dr Ella,
I hope you=92ve been doing well. This is Asad Ikram, I had the pleasure of =
working under your supervision during my MSc Data Analytics dissertation at=
 Portsmouth, =93Sentiment Analysis of Public Reaction to UK Economic Polici=
es.=94
I=92m currently exploring PhD opportunities in the area of AI-driven social=
 media analysis and came across your fascinating project, =93The Algorithmi=
c Gaze: Mapping Social Media Trends and Their Impact Using Artificial Intel=
ligence.=94 The topic aligns perfectly with my academic background and prof=
essional experience of 5+ years, especially my recent work in large-scale d=
ata engineering and social media analytics for UK government projects at Fl=
uency (M+C Saatchi), where I built pipelines for trend detection, public se=
ntiment measurement, and algorithmic transparency.
While I noticed this particular PhD is self-funded, I wanted to ask if ther=
e are any funded openings or upcoming projects within your team or the Scho=
ol of Computing that focus on AI, LLMs, or computational social science. I=
=92m particularly keen on research that bridges machine learning, social be=
havior, and digital governance. A direction that has been central to my wor=
k and Chevening vision since my MSc.
I=92ve attached my CV and can share my recent research proposal if helpful.=
 I=92d be grateful for any guidance on potential funded opportunities or di=
rections to explore within the department.
Warm regards,
Asad Ikram
Chevening Scholar | MSc Data Analytics (Distinction, Portsmouth)
